// Embalm [CR#702.128a]: "Embalm [cost]" means "[cost], Exile this card from
// your graveyard: Create a token that's a copy of it, except it's a white
// Zombie. Embalm only as a sorcery." Scavenge's graveyard twin ([CR#702.97a]):
// same activated-from-graveyard, exile-self, sorcery-speed shell — only the
// effect differs (a token copy in place of the +1/+1-counter grant).
//
// Pieces (all over existing primitives — no engine gap):
//   - from: Graveyard [CR#702.128a] — the zone-of-function seam ([CR#113.6]);
//     the ability functions only while the card is in a graveyard.
//   - cost: the printed [cost] THEN exile this card. `Splice(Param(0))` inlines
//     the printed cost components ahead of the fixed `Do(Move(This, Exile))`
//     (Scavenge's exile-self, [CR#701.13]) at read time — one flat cost list.
//   - window: SorcerySpeed [CR#602.5d] — "only as a sorcery".
//   - effect: `Create(1, Copy(source: SelfCard, ...))` — a token copy of the
//     exiled card ([CR#707.1]) EXCEPT it's white ([CR#707.9]: `Colors(Set([White]))`)
//     and a Zombie in addition to its other types (`Subtypes(Add(Zombie))`).
//     A token has no mana cost slot ([CR#111.3,707.2]), so "no mana cost" needs
//     no exception; the source's printed P/T rides through unchanged.
(
    name: "Embalm",
    template: "embalm ${0}",
    kinds: [KeywordAbility],
    params: [Cost],
    body: Composite(
        name: "Embalm",
        abilities: [Activated(
            from: Graveyard,
            cost: [Splice(Param(0)), Do(Move(This, Exile))],
            window: SorcerySpeed,
            effect: Create(1, Copy(source: SelfCard, exceptions: [
                Modify(Colors(Set([White]))),
                Modify(Subtypes(Add(Zombie))),
            ])),
        )],
    ),
)
